<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_PristineFirehawkCrestfeather.xml · 2026-11-13
  Owner, 2026-11-13: "Pristine ... Crestfeather is a valuable object of beauty to further reward the hunt." Name corrected the
  same day: "No, I meant Firehawk". Dropped by a butchered RM_FireHawk at a flat 35 % (RM_ButcherTrophyExtension on the race,
  Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RM_PyrelandsFauna.xml; rolled by ButcherTrophyPatch, Source/FireHawkRewards.cs).

  Built like Core's one small item of beauty, Anomaly's GoldenCube (Items_Various.xml, read through RimSage): a plain Item,
  ItemsMisc, Beauty in statBases. Items count toward a room's beauty wherever they lie, unless stored where the storage
  ignores stored beauty (BeautyUtility.CellBeauty); a stack counts once (Thing.GetBeauty does not scale with stackCount).

  Numbers (delegated: design, 2026-11-13):
    Beauty        40   a little under a normal-quality small sculpture (SculptureSmall, Beauty 50 x quality): an art-grade
                       find that needs no artist; far below the cube's 400, which is a psychic artefact.
    MarketValue  350   about twice the hawk itself (180), under a thrumbo horn (800): at 35 % a hunted hawk is worth ~120
                       more on average, which is the reason to hunt it.
    stackLimit     5   small, as Anomaly's Shard; one feather already gives a room its whole beauty.
    Flammability   0   grown on a bird that carries live embers; on a map that is always burning anything less is ash.
    HitPoints, DeteriorationRate as the thrumbo horn (Core's animal trophy): left outdoors it slowly loses its "pristine".

  PLACEHOLDER ART: no crestfeather art exists (artpipe searched 2026-11-13: no job, no sheet). The texPath below borrows
  vanilla's thrumbo horn tinted ember-orange until the queued sprite lands
  (infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/pyrelands_firehawk_crestfeather_2026-11-13.csv, filed against this vanilla slot, the
  route the art gate allows for a def drawing a vanilla stand-in); on acceptance the render installs at the def's own path
  (regen_eligibility.own_path: Things/Item/Special/RM_PristineFirehawkCrestfeather/RM_PristineFirehawkCrestfeather), texPath
  moves there and the colour line goes.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>RM_PristineFirehawkCrestfeather</defName>
    <label>pristine firehawk crestfeather</label>
    <description>The crest feather of a fire-hawk, taken whole. Its vanes shade from ash-grey at the quill to a living ember-orange at the tip, and in any light it seems to glow from inside. It will not burn. A rare find even among the people who hunt fire-hawks, and an object of real beauty in any room.</description>
    <thingClass>ThingWithComps</thingClass>
    <category>Item</category>
    <drawerType>MapMeshOnly</drawerType>
    <altitudeLayer>Item</altitudeLayer>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <alwaysHaulable>true</alwaysHaulable>
    <drawGUIOverlay>true</drawGUIOverlay>
    <useHitPoints>true</useHitPoints>
    <pathCost>14</pathCost>
    <stackLimit>5</stackLimit>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- PLACEHOLDER ART: vanilla thrumbo horn, tinted. See the header. -->
      <texPath>Things/Item/Special/ThrumboHorn</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <color>(230,120,40)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Beauty>40</Beauty>
      <MarketValue>350</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.05</Mass>
      <MaxHitPoints>150</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0.5</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ItemsMisc</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Forbiddable" />
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
